<div align="center">

# ✨ AI Folder Sorter

### Sort your open tabs into smart folders with one click — powered by AI.

A [Zen Browser](https://zen-browser.app) mod that automatically categorizes your tabs into color-coded tab groups using AI. Works with Gemini, Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

[![Zen Browser](https://img.shields.io/badge/Zen%20Browser-128%2B-blueviolet?style=for-the-badge&logo=firefox)](https://zen-browser.app)
[![Sine](https://img.shields.io/badge/Sine-Mod%20Loader-orange?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/CosmoCreeper/Sine)
[![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.0.0-brightgreen?style=for-the-badge)](CHANGELOG.md)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue?style=for-the-badge)](LICENSE)

</div>

---

## ✨ Features

- **🤖 Multi-provider AI** — Gemini, Ollama (local), or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Groq, OpenAI, LM Studio, vLLM)
- **📐 Rules system** — Pin domains to folders (`github.com → 💻 Dev`). Rules run before AI, saving tokens and giving you deterministic control
- **🖱️ Right-click menu** — Right-click any tab → "Always sort `[host]` into..." to add a rule instantly
- **🎨 Smart colors** — AI-suggested colors validated against Zen's palette
- **🔀 Fuzzy matching** — Case/whitespace-insensitive folder matching prevents duplicates
- **⏱️ Fetch timeout** — 60-second timeout prevents stuck buttons if AI hangs
- **📦 Auto-batching** — Large tab sets (>100) split into batches for token limits
- **🆘 Fallback button** — Draggable floating button appears if sidebar injection fails
- **⌨️ Keyboard shortcut** — `Ctrl+Shift+S` / `Cmd+Shift+S`
- **↩️ Undo** — Notifications include Undo to revert the last sort

---

## 📦 Installation

### Prerequisites

- [Zen Browser](https://zen-browser.app) (Firefox 128+ fork)
- [Sine mod loader](https://github.com/CosmoCreeper/Sine) installed in Zen

### Install

1. Download the latest release from [Releases](../../releases)
2. Extract to your Sine mods folder:
   - **Windows**: `%APPDATA%\zen\Sine\mods\ai-folder-sorter\`
   - **macOS**: `~/Library/Application Support/Zen/Sine/mods/ai-folder-sorter/`
   - **Linux**: `~/.zen/Sine/mods/ai-folder-sorter/`
3. The folder should look like:
   ```
   ai-folder-sorter/
   ├── ai-folder-sorter.uc.mjs    ← MUST be .uc.mjs (not .uc.js)
   ├── modules/
   │   ├── config.mjs
   │   ├── tabs.mjs
   │   ├── rules.mjs
   │   ├── ai.mjs
   │   ├── groups.mjs
   │   ├── notify.mjs
   │   ├── browser-ui.mjs
   │   ├── browser-hooks.mjs
   │   └── click-handler.mjs
   ├── userChrome.css
   ├── theme.json
   └── preferences.json
   ```

   > ⚠️ **Critical:** The script file MUST have the `.uc.mjs` extension. Sine's loader only processes `.uc.mjs` files — a `.uc.js` file will be silently ignored.

4. Restart Zen Browser

### Verify it's working

Open the Browser Console (`Ctrl+Shift+J` / `Cmd+Shift+J`) and look for:

```
[AI-FolderSorter] Script loaded (v1.0.0). Ready to initialize.
[AI-FolderSorter] ✅ [AI-FolderSorter] initialized successfully! (v1.0.0)
```

You should see a ✨ wand icon in your sidebar separator. Click it to sort your tabs!

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

1. **Configure your AI provider** — Settings → AI Folder Sorter:
   - **Provider**: `custom` (Groq) / `gemini` / `ollama`
   - **API Key**: Your key (Groq `gsk_...`, Gemini `AIza...`)
   - **Model**: e.g. `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` (Groq) or `gemini-2.5-flash` (Gemini)

2. **Click the ✨ wand button** in your sidebar

3. **Watch your tabs get sorted!**
   ```
   ✨ Sorted 24 tabs into 5 folder(s)! (8 via rules, 16 via AI)
   ```

---

## 🤖 AI Providers

### Groq (recommended — fast & free)

1. Get a free API key at [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com)
2. Provider = `custom` · API Key = `gsk_...` · Model = `llama-3.3-70b-versatile`

### Google Gemini

1. Get an API key at [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com)
2. Provider = `gemini` · API Key = `AIza...` · Model = `gemini-2.5-flash`

### Local Ollama (no cloud, no API key)

1. Install [Ollama](https://ollama.com) → `ollama pull llama3.1:8b`
2. Provider = `ollama` · Model = `llama3.1:8b`

### Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint

Works with LM Studio, vLLM, text-generation-webui, OpenAI itself, etc.
- Provider = `custom` · Endpoint = your URL · Model = your model name

---

## 📐 Rules System

Rules pin specific domains to specific folders, bypassing the AI entirely. Great for sites you visit frequently.

### Add a rule

**Right-click any tab** → "Always sort `[hostname]` into..." → pick a folder (or create a new one).

Or edit the pref directly in `about:config` → `zen.ai-folder-sorter.rules-json`:

```json
[
  {"domain": "github.com", "folder": "💻 Dev", "color": "blue"},
  {"domain": "amazon.com", "folder": "🛒 Shopping", "color": "pink"},
  {"domain": "reddit.com", "folder": "📱 Social", "color": "purple"}
]
```

### How matching works

- Rules match against the tab's hostname
- Parent-domain matching: a rule for `github.com` also matches `docs.github.com`, `api.github.com`, etc.
- More specific rules take priority

### Rules vs AI

1. **Rules phase** — matched tabs go straight to their folder (no AI call)
2. **AI phase** — only unmatched tabs are sent to the AI

If all tabs match rules, the AI isn't called at all.

---

## ⚙️ Configuration

Settings are in Zen → Settings → AI Folder Sorter.

| Setting | Description | Default |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| AI Provider | `custom`, `gemini`, or `ollama` | `custom` |
| API Key | Your API key | _(empty)_ |
| Model Name | Model to use | `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` |
| Custom Endpoint | OpenAI-compatible URL | `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions` |
| Enable AI Emojis | Prepend emojis to folder names | `true` |
| Ollama Endpoint | Local Ollama URL | `http://localhost:11434/api/chat` |
| Ollama Model | Local model name | `llama3.1:8b` |

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
ai-folder-sorter.uc.mjs          Entry point (~145 lines)
├── modules/
│   ├── config.mjs               Constants, CONFIG, log helper
│   ├── tabs.mjs                 Tab extraction, DOM cache
│   ├── rules.mjs                Domain→folder rules
│   ├── ai.mjs                   Prompt, request, parsing
│   ├── groups.mjs               Folder creation strategies
│   ├── notify.mjs               Notifications + toast fallback
│   ├── browser-ui.mjs           Button injection, workspace hooks
│   ├── browser-hooks.mjs        Right-click context menu
│   └── click-handler.mjs        Main sort pipeline
├── userChrome.css               Button styles + animations
├── theme.json                   Sine mod metadata
└── preferences.json             Settings panel definition
```

Each module has a single responsibility. The entry point is a thin orchestrator that imports everything and wires up initialization.

---

## 🔧 Troubleshooting

### The button doesn't appear

1. **Open the Browser Console** (`Ctrl+Shift+J` / `Cmd+Shift+J`)
2. **Search for `[AI-FolderSorter]`**

**If you see ZERO log entries** → the script isn't loading. The file must be named `.uc.mjs`, not `.uc.js`. Sine only loads `.uc.mjs` files.

**If you see logs but no button** → check the readiness line:
```
[AI-FolderSorter] Readiness: gBrowser=true cmd=true sep=false periph=true ws=true
```
- `gBrowser=false` → wait a few seconds for Zen to finish loading
- `sep=false` → button will fall back to `#tabbrowser-arrowscrollbox-periphery` (still works)
- `ws=false` → button appears but won't auto-reinject on workspace switch

**If sidebar injection completely fails** → a floating purple ✨ button appears in the top-right corner after 8 seconds. Use it to trigger sorts while you debug.

To hide the floating button: set `zen.ai-folder-sorter.hide-fallback` to `true` in `about:config` and restart.

### Sort fails with "AI returned invalid JSON"

- Try a more capable model (`llama-3.3-70b-versatile` instead of `llama3.1:8b`)
- Reduce the number of open tabs
- Check your API key and endpoint

### Sort is slow

- **Ollama**: first sort after launch takes a few seconds (model loads into VRAM). Subsequent sorts are fast.
- **Cloud provider**: check your internet connection
- **100+ tabs**: automatically split into batches — each batch is a separate API call

### Tabs go to the wrong folder

- **Add a rule** for the site (right-click → "Always sort into...")
- **Try a different model** — `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` and `gemini-2.5-pro` are most accurate

